1
00:00:00,035 --> 00:00:03,079
Why does every GTA, even GTA 6,

2
00:00:03,079 --> 00:00:04,785
have you running from the cops?

3
00:00:04,785 --> 00:00:07,683
Because back in 1995, a game about chasing

4
00:00:07,683 --> 00:00:09,185
criminals broke.

5
00:00:09,185 --> 00:00:10,790
And that bug saved it.

6
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:11,500
Here's how.

7
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,205
It's 1995 in Dundee, Scotland.

8
00:00:14,205 --> 00:00:16,755
DMA Design, the studio behind Lemmings,

9
00:00:16,755 --> 00:00:17,960
starts a new game.

10
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,470
It's called Race'n'Chase,

11
00:00:19,470 --> 00:00:21,535
and it's planned to take eighteen months.

12
00:00:21,535 --> 00:00:23,556
In it, you play a police officer chasing

13
00:00:23,556 --> 00:00:24,470
criminals.

14
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:26,500
But there's a problem: it's dull.

15
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,825
One developer later calls it “awful…

16
00:00:28,825 --> 00:00:30,005
too sim-y.”

17
00:00:30,005 --> 00:00:31,845
So the people above the team keep trying

18
00:00:31,845 --> 00:00:33,205
to shut it down.

19
00:00:33,205 --> 00:00:35,315
Then, something breaks.

20
00:00:35,315 --> 00:00:37,452
The police cars stop following you and start

21
00:00:37,452 --> 00:00:39,530
trying to drive straight through you.

22
00:00:39,530 --> 00:00:40,345
They ram.

23
00:00:40,345 --> 00:00:41,240
They chase.

24
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:42,470
They don't let go.

25
00:00:42,470 --> 00:00:44,380
And suddenly, it's fun.

26
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:46,475
So the team flips the whole game.

27
00:00:46,475 --> 00:00:47,815
You're not the cop anymore.

28
00:00:47,815 --> 00:00:49,775
Now you're the one being chased.

29
00:00:49,775 --> 00:00:52,061
Of course, the eighteen months turn into

30
00:00:52,061 --> 00:00:52,565
thirty.

31
00:00:52,565 --> 00:00:55,360
Until finally, in November 1997,

32
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:56,930
it ships with a new name:

33
00:00:56,930 --> 00:00:58,635
Grand Theft Auto.

34
00:00:59,670 --> 00:01:02,005
And every GTA since is built around that

35
00:01:02,005 --> 00:01:02,870
chase.

36
00:01:02,870 --> 00:01:04,115
The wanted stars.

37
00:01:04,115 --> 00:01:05,075
The sirens.

38
00:01:05,075 --> 00:01:05,935
The running.

39
00:01:05,935 --> 00:01:06,820
Don't believe me?

40
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:09,255
Open GTA Online and buy an arcade.

41
00:01:09,255 --> 00:01:11,880
One of the machines is called Race and Chase.

42
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:13,650
So that's why you're always running.

43
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:15,895
The whole series started with a bug.

44
00:01:15,895 --> 00:01:17,150
And GTA 6?

45
00:01:17,150 --> 00:01:19,300
It opens with Lucia already caught.

46
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:20,868
So who's chasing who now?
